dnsx
Usage: dnsx -l FILE [-resp] [-silent]   |   dnsx -d DOMAIN -w LIST

A fast dns toolkit. Resolve a list of names to addresses, show their records,
or brute-force subdomains from a wordlist. The bridge between a list of names
(from subfinder) and the live hosts you actually probe.

	-l FILE     resolve every name in this file
	-resp       show the response value, not just the name
	-a          name the A record explicitly -- the default, so usually omit it
	-aaaa -cname  ask for other record types instead
	-d -w LIST  brute-force subdomains of a domain from a wordlist
	-silent     clean output for piping

Only against domains you are authorised to assess.

See also: subfinder, httpx
